<title>USA: Energen names new president/CEO.</title>
<headline>Energen names new president/CEO.</headline>
<dateline>BIRMINGHAM, Ala. 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Energen Corp said Wednesday it elected William Michael Warren Jr. president and chief executive officer, succeeding Rex Lysinger as CEO of the energy company.</p>
<p>Warren has served as company president since 1991.</p>
<p>Energen said Lysinger will continue to serve as board chairman until the first of the year, when he will retire from the company.   Lysinger will continue as a director, completing</p>
<p>his present term in 2000, the company said.</p>
<p>In October 1995, Warren was elected CEO of Alagasco, the company's gas utility subsidiary, and Taurus Exploration, the company's oil and gas exploration and production subsidiary.</p>
